<!-- =========================================================
     OUR APPROACH TO INCLUSION
========================================================= -->

<section class="inclusion-section">

  <div class="inclusion-container">

    <!-- Section Header -->
    <div class="inclusion-header">

      <span class="inclusion-badge">
        Inclusion in Action
      </span>

      <h2>
        Our Approach to Inclusion
      </h2>

      <p>
        We believe every child deserves the opportunity to experience the joy of sports
      </p>

    </div>


    <!-- Inclusion Cards -->
    <div class="inclusion-grid">


      <!-- Card 1 -->
      <article class="inclusion-card">

        <div class="inclusion-icon inclusion-icon-purple">
          <span>♿</span>
        </div>

        <h3>
          Adaptive Sports Programs
        </h3>

        <p>
          Our adaptive sports programs are specifically designed for children with
          intellectual disabilities. We modify equipment, rules, and training methods
          to ensure every child can participate meaningfully and experience success
          at their own pace.
        </p>

        <p>
          Coaches trained in adaptive physical education work closely with each
          child, building skills progressively while celebrating every milestone —
          big or small.
        </p>

      </article>


      <!-- Card 2 -->
      <article class="inclusion-card">

        <div class="inclusion-icon inclusion-icon-pink">
          <span>♧</span>
        </div>

        <h3>
          Unified Training Sessions
        </h3>

        <p>
          In our unified sessions, typical children and children with disabilities train
          together, breaking down barriers and building empathy. These sessions
          foster mutual understanding, friendship, and a sense of belonging that
          extends beyond the sports field.
        </p>

        <p>
          Parents consistently report that unified training helps their children
          develop compassion, patience, and teamwork skills that benefit them in all
          areas of life.
        </p>

      </article>


      <!-- Card 3 -->
      <article class="inclusion-card">

        <div class="inclusion-icon inclusion-icon-orange">
          <span>♡</span>
        </div>

        <h3>
          Individualized Support Plans
        </h3>

        <p>
          Every child receives an individualized support plan developed in
          consultation with parents, coaches, and our special education team. These
          plans outline goals, accommodations, and communication strategies
          tailored to each child's unique needs.
        </p>

        <p>
          We regularly review and adjust these plans to ensure continuous progress
          and address any challenges that arise during training or camp sessions.
        </p>

      </article>


      <!-- Card 4 -->
      <article class="inclusion-card">

        <div class="inclusion-icon inclusion-icon-yellow">
          <span>♢</span>
        </div>

        <h3>
          Safe &amp; Supportive Environment
        </h3>

        <p>
          Safety is foundational to everything we do. Our facilities are designed with
          accessibility in mind, and our staff includes trained medical professionals,
          counselors, and support personnel available around the clock during camp
          sessions.
        </p>

        <p>
          We maintain low coach-to-child ratios, conduct regular safety drills, and
          follow strict protocols to ensure every child feels secure, respected, and
          valued.
        </p>

      </article>


    </div>

  </div>

</section>





